{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":62792,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"afd9d25b-c1a0-5b7d-a675-5d412de41041","total_cost_usd":0.5426650000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11737,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":6034,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11737,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6034,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11737},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6115,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006205,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":6034,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11737,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.53646,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-j2-reviewer-fable-46\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:e388fb42ef8a65964476\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description states each independent unit (site_id) appears exactly once and that there are no repeat visits, subplots, or sub-samples, so the 100 rows are 100 separate sites.\",\"observed_value\":\"one row per site_id; no nesting or repeat visits\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":11,\"end_line\":12,\"quoted_text\":\"- `site_id`: the permanent identifier of the restoration site, FD-001 through FD-100.\\n  Each identifier appears on exactly one line of the file.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":20,\"end_line\":22,\"quoted_text\":\"There are no repeat visits, no subplots and no sub-samples anywhere in the file. Nothing\\nis nested inside anything else: the survey recorded one line per site, so the 100 lines\\nare 100 separate sites, and the cover-class tally is a tally over separate sites.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":25,\"quoted_text\":\"Independent unit column: site_id\"}]},{\"description\":\"The input CSV contains exactly 100 data rows with unique site identifiers FD-001 through FD-100 (header on line 1; first and last data rows shown). No site_id repeats.\",\"observed_value\":\"100 unique site_id values, FD-001..FD-100\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":2,\"quoted_text\":\"site_id,shore_marker_km,foredune_width_m,sand_ph,cover_class\\nFD-001,4.2,14,8.1,sparse\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":101,\"end_line\":101,\"quoted_text\":\"FD-100,350.7,51,8.7,sparse\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow enforces uniqueness of the independent unit: read_sites raises a ValueError if any site_id appears more than once, so a repeated-unit entry cannot silently reach the test.\",\"observed_value\":\"duplicate site_id guard present in read_sites\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":37,\"end_line\":39,\"quoted_text\":\"        if site in seen:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"site_id appears more than once: {0}\\\".format(site))\\n        seen.add(site)\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":27,\"end_line\":27,\"quoted_text\":\"    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return the survey rows, checking that every site appears exactly once.\\\"\\\"\\\"\"}]},{\"description\":\"The tally and test consume each row exactly once with no resampling, joining, or expansion: tally_classes runs a single Counter pass over the rows, and stats.chisquare is applied to those per-site counts. The reported n of 100 equals the number of unique sites, and the counts 48+39+13 sum to 100.\",\"observed_value\":\"n = 100; counts 48 sparse / 39 patchy / 13 closed; chi-square(2) = 6.0000, p = 0.049787 (arithmetic independently verified: 2.4 + 2.7 + 0.9 = 6.0)\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":46,\"end_line\":49,\"quoted_text\":\"def tally_classes(rows: List[Dict[str, str]]) -> np.ndarray:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Count sites per cover class, in the fixed reporting order.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    counts = Counter(row[\\\"cover_class\\\"].strip() for row in rows)\\n    return np.array([counts[name] for name in CLASS_ORDER], dtype=float)\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":6,\"end_line\":6,\"quoted_text\":\"- Independent units: 100 restoration sites, one row per site (site identifiers verified unique).\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":27,\"end_line\":27,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Chi-square goodness-of-fit on 100 independent restoration sites (one classification per site): chi-square(2) = 6.0000, p = 0.049787, Cohen's w = 0.2449; the 2024 cover-class composition (48 sparse / 39 patchy / 13 closed) differs from the 2019 reference composition of 0.60 / 0.30 / 0.10 at alpha = 0.05.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"Strongest opposing consideration: the 100 sites lie sequentially along a single 350 km coastline, so spatial autocorrelation between neighbouring sites could in principle weaken the independence assumed by the chi-square test. However, this is a spatial-dependence concern, not repeated entry of the same authorized unit, and the description asserts sites are at least 3.5 km apart and are separate units; it therefore does not demonstrate the target issue class.\",\"observed_value\":\"sites spaced every 3.5 km along one contiguous coast\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":4,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"Field crews walked a 350 km stretch of open coast and stopped at a fixed marker every\\n3.5 km, which gave 100 restoration sites separated by at least 3.5 km of shoreline.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The reported p-value (0.049787) sits just below alpha = 0.05, so the rejection decision is fragile; but the value is arithmetically correct for the observed counts and its marginality is not evidence of any unit entering the procedure more than once.\",\"observed_value\":\"p = 0.049787 vs alpha = 0.05\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":23,\"end_line\":25,\"quoted_text\":\"- p-value: 0.049787\\n- Effect size (Cohen's w): 0.2449\\n- Decision at alpha = 0.05: reject the reference composition.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I actively searched for any way an independent unit (site_id) could enter the chi-square procedure more than once: (1) scanned all 100 data rows of data/input.csv for duplicate site_id values — FD-001 through FD-100 each appear exactly once; (2) traced the workflow end to end for row duplication mechanisms (merges, appends, resampling, bootstrapping, per-subunit expansion) — read_sites performs one pass with an explicit duplicate-site_id guard that raises ValueError, and tally_classes does a single Counter pass, so each row contributes exactly one count; (3) cross-checked the reported n = 100 against the number of unique sites and recomputed the statistic (contributions 144/60 + 81/30 + 9/10 = 6.0, df = 2, p = exp(-3) ≈ 0.049787, w = sqrt(6/100) ≈ 0.2449), which matches the report exactly, confirming no inflated count reached the test. All attempts to demonstrate repeated-unit entry failed.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-j2-reviewer-fable-46","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:e388fb42ef8a65964476","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description states each independent unit (site_id) appears exactly once and that there are no repeat visits, subplots, or sub-samples, so the 100 rows are 100 separate sites.","observed_value":"one row per site_id; no nesting or repeat visits","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":11,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"- `site_id`: the permanent identifier of the restoration site, FD-001 through FD-100.\n  Each identifier appears on exactly one line of the file."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":20,"end_line":22,"quoted_text":"There are no repeat visits, no subplots and no sub-samples anywhere in the file. Nothing\nis nested inside anything else: the survey recorded one line per site, so the 100 lines\nare 100 separate sites, and the cover-class tally is a tally over separate sites."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: site_id"}]},{"description":"The input CSV contains exactly 100 data rows with unique site identifiers FD-001 through FD-100 (header on line 1; first and last data rows shown). No site_id repeats.","observed_value":"100 unique site_id values, FD-001..FD-100","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"site_id,shore_marker_km,foredune_width_m,sand_ph,cover_class\nFD-001,4.2,14,8.1,sparse"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":101,"end_line":101,"quoted_text":"FD-100,350.7,51,8.7,sparse"}]},{"description":"The workflow enforces uniqueness of the independent unit: read_sites raises a ValueError if any site_id appears more than once, so a repeated-unit entry cannot silently reach the test.","observed_value":"duplicate site_id guard present in read_sites","source_spans":