ld in principle weaken the independence assumed by the chi-square test. However, this is a spatial-dependence concern, not repeated entry of the same authorized unit, and the description asserts sites are at least 3.5 km apart and are separate units; it therefore does not demonstrate the target issue class.","observed_value":"sites spaced every 3.5 km along one contiguous coast","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":4,"end_line":5,"quoted_text":"Field crews walked a 350 km stretch of open coast and stopped at a fixed marker every\n3.5 km, which gave 100 restoration sites separated by at least 3.5 km of shoreline."}]},{"description":"The reported p-value (0.049787) sits just below alpha = 0.05, so the rejection decision is fragile; but the value is arithmetically correct for the observed counts and its marginality is not evidence of any unit entering the procedure more than once.","observed_value":"p = 0.049787 vs alpha = 0.05","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":23,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"- p-value: 0.049787\n- Effect size (Cohen's w): 0.2449\n- Decision at alpha = 0.05: reject the reference composition."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I actively searched for any way an independent unit (site_id) could enter the chi-square procedure more than once: (1) scanned all 100 data rows of data/input.csv for duplicate site_id values — FD-001 through FD-100 each appear exactly once; (2) traced the workflow end to end for row duplication mechanisms (merges, appends, resampling, bootstrapping, per-subunit expansion) — read_sites performs one pass with an explicit duplicate-site_id guard that raises ValueError, and tally_classes does a single Counter pass, so each row contributes exactly one count; (3) cross-checked the reported n = 100 against the number of unique sites and recomputed the statistic (contributions 144/60 + 81/30 + 9/10 = 6.0, df = 2, p = exp(-3) ≈ 0.049787, w = sqrt(6/100) ≈ 0.2449), which matches the report exactly, confirming no inflated count reached the test. All attempts to demonstrate repeated-unit entry failed.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":30969,"ttft_stream_ms":2466,"time_to_request_ms":10,"type":"result","duration_ms":61635,"uuid":"c511b3dc-3e04-4338-a7ad-af5795ef5587"}
